# Nested instruction-named files that are not directory instructions, one per line as
# <repo-name>:<glob>. repo-name is the repository directory's basename; glob is a bash
# case pattern matched against the repo-relative path, so * crosses /. harness-doctor
# check 5 skips a matching nested CLAUDE.md (not an '@AGENTS.md' stub) or nested
# AGENTS.md (no sibling pointer). The root path AGENTS.md marks a repo that needs no
# instruction file at all, so the "active repo(s) missing AGENTS.md" note stops naming
# it. A bare * matches the root path too. A # after optional leading whitespace starts
# a comment; blank lines are ignored; a malformed line is reported on stderr and ignored.
# Copy to <overlay>/instruction-file-exempt and edit.
#
# A host overlay file imported by absolute path:
example-repo:docs/overlay/CLAUDE.md
# Archived or frozen release text:
example-repo:archive/*
# Captured evidence copies, anywhere in the tree:
example-other-repo:*/evidence/*
# A small repo, or a fork that follows its upstream's convention, that needs no AGENTS.md:
example-fork:AGENTS.md
